1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:02,240
This series was created
for entertainment purposes.

2
00:00:02,240 --> 00:00:05,680
The characters, actions, locations,
dialogue, languages, ceremonies,

3
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:08,120
and artistic elements depicted in this series

4
00:00:08,120 --> 00:00:10,040
are fictional and based on imagination,

5
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:13,920
incorporating the beauty
of the region's diverse cultures,

6
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:18,400
including those
of Lanna, Myanmar, the Tai peoples, and China.

7
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,560
It is not intended to disrespect any history,

8
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:23,600
ethnic group, organization, profession,
or group of individuals.

9
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:26,040
Viewer discretion is advised.

10
00:00:26,040 --> 00:00:28,160
[Previously]
<i>You've finally returned to Wiang Kaew.</i>

11
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:31,560
<i>But your stay is only temporary, Your Highness.</i>

12
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:33,760
<i>I'll do everything I can
to win Father's approval,</i>

13
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:36,720
<i>so I can stay in Ullavee for good.</i>

14
00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:41,680
<i>Princess Maneethip did have a lover,
just as you suspected.</i>

15
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:44,600
<i>Then tell me what happened to General In Saeng?</i>

16
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:46,800
<i>General In Saeng...</i>

17
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:50,440
<i>died of jungle fever two days ago
while stationed at the border.</i>

18
00:00:50,440 --> 00:00:54,040
<i>From now on, you must watch your every move.</i>

19
00:00:54,040 --> 00:00:56,520
<i>Remember everything I've taught you.</i>

20
00:00:56,520 --> 00:00:59,600
<i>- You'll be presented to the King tomorrow.
- Yes.</i>

21
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:28,800
- Dried peep flowers, my lady.
- This tobacco blend is called Kiyo.

22
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:32,560
It's made with loose tobacco,
ground tamarind bark,

23
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:35,520
and dried peep flowers.

24
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:37,760
The King is very fond of this blend.

25
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:42,360
It soothes the throat when smoked,
and leaves the breath smelling fresh.

26
00:01:43,080 --> 00:01:48,680
You'll be helping me roll tobacco by hand,
and prepare leaf wraps.

27
00:01:48,680 --> 00:01:54,400
You'll also serve tea,
snacks, and drinks to the King.

28
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:59,440
- I'm nervous. I'm afraid I'll make mistakes.
- There's nothing to fear.

29
00:01:59,440 --> 00:02:04,480
Just follow what I've taught you,
and you'll be fine.

30
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:10,800
<i>Wiang Kaew can bring you as much harm
as it can bring you gain.</i>

31
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:12,880
<i>So be wise.</i>

32
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:16,520
Don't even think of doing anything
you shouldn't.

33
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:37,720
Lady Homjan and Fongnuan have come
to serve Your Majesty.

34
00:02:37,720 --> 00:02:39,160
Come in.

35
00:04:22,080 --> 00:04:28,520
[Tears of Love]

36
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:39,960
<i>Breathe in. Breathe out.</i>

37
00:04:39,960 --> 00:04:44,200
<i>Breathe in. Breathe out.</i>

38
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:48,080
<i>Breathe in. Breathe out.</i>

39
00:04:49,880 --> 00:04:53,160
- I pay my respects to you, Your Majesty.
- I pay my respects to you, Your Majesty.

40
00:04:57,520 --> 00:05:02,480
I've brought the new lady-in-waiting
to serve Your Majesty.

41
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:46,000
I am Fongnuan.

42
00:05:46,800 --> 00:05:50,440
I've prepared leaf wraps and
hand-rolled Kiyo for Your Majesty.

43
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:53,160
Did you make these yourself?

44
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:56,360
Yes, Your Majesty.

45
00:05:57,600 --> 00:06:02,080
Had you not told me,
I'd have thought Homjan made them.

46
00:06:06,520 --> 00:06:11,600
I'm not nearly as skilled as Lady Homjan,
Your Majesty.

47
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:18,560
Your new apprentice is a quick learner.

48
00:06:18,560 --> 00:06:21,560
And modest, too.

49
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:24,800
You must be pleased with her, Homjan.

50
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:30,480
She still has much to learn, Your Majesty.
Please forgive her if she makes mistakes.

51
00:06:30,480 --> 00:06:35,640
I'll make sure she meets
Your Majesty's expectations.

52
00:06:35,640 --> 00:06:38,360
Fongnuan, look at your Head Lady-in-Waiting.

53
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:44,160
It's only your first day,
and she's already defending you.

54
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:51,320
Fongnuan doesn't ask for much, Your Majesty.
But she's eager to learn.

55
00:06:51,320 --> 00:06:52,840
On her first day at Wiang Kaew,

56
00:06:52,840 --> 00:06:56,160
she made it clear
she had no desire for a high position.

57
00:06:56,160 --> 00:06:59,200
She only wants to get through each day.

58
00:07:01,280 --> 00:07:06,000
Homjan tells me you know acupressure.

59
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:09,120
I've been having pain
in my neck and shoulders.

60
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:11,720
Sometimes the pain reaches my head.

61
00:07:11,720 --> 00:07:16,000
Do you think you could help ease it?

62
00:07:28,120 --> 00:07:30,760
If Your Majesty permits,

63
00:07:30,760 --> 00:07:36,040
I'll do everything I can to help.

64
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:55,400
<i>The King's body is sacred.
He possesses immense spiritual power.</i>

65
00:07:55,400 --> 00:08:00,160
<i>His body is protected by incantations.
Not just anyone may touch him.</i>

66
00:08:00,160 --> 00:08:05,680
<i>That is why the King's physicians and masseurs
are all men.</i>

67
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:11,440
<i>As a woman,
you must first offer popped rice and flowers.</i>

68
00:08:11,440 --> 00:08:13,800
<i>Ask permission and forgiveness for any offense.</i>

69
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:19,120
<i>Otherwise, if his power overwhelms you,
it could enter your body and harm you.</i>

70
00:08:26,520 --> 00:08:31,840
<i>My lady, what if I accidentally hurt the King?</i>

71
00:08:31,840 --> 00:08:34,280
<i>Will I be executed?</i>

72
00:08:35,520 --> 00:08:38,800
<i>Be very careful. Don't press the wrong spot.</i>

73
00:09:40,280 --> 00:09:42,360
You've only pressed a few points,

74
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:48,920
yet the pain and tension in my head
have already eased.

75
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:54,640
That is a valuable skill. I'm pleased.

76
00:10:20,880 --> 00:10:24,480
What are you doing
about the bandits stealing from the granaries?

77
00:10:24,480 --> 00:10:29,080
I've sent soldiers to patrol the area,
and keep a close watch on the granaries.

78
00:10:29,080 --> 00:10:32,400
I assure you it won't happen again.

79
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:35,520
That's not enough.

80
00:10:36,160 --> 00:10:38,320
You must plan further ahead.

81
00:10:40,160 --> 00:10:45,360
The dry season is almost over.
We must do more than guard the granaries.

82
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:49,600
We must prepare for the rainy season...

83
00:10:49,600 --> 00:10:53,480
and ensure Ullavee has enough food and supplies

84
00:10:53,480 --> 00:10:55,600
to last the entire year.

85
00:10:59,520 --> 00:11:04,800
Thank you for your guidance, Father.
I still have much to learn from you.

86
00:11:31,520 --> 00:11:36,560
<i>The drum sounds once,
marking the third watch.</i>

87
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:40,840
<i>It's already half past one.</i>

88
00:11:41,920 --> 00:11:44,760
<i>Another important part of your duty...</i>

89
00:11:44,760 --> 00:11:47,880
<i>is looking after His Majesty's health.</i>

90
00:11:47,880 --> 00:11:50,880
<i>You must help me care for him
and watch over him.</i>

91
00:11:50,880 --> 00:11:56,280
<i>Make sure he doesn't fall ill
or do anything that harms his health.</i>

92
00:11:57,360 --> 00:12:00,000
I pay my respects to you, Your Majesty.

93
00:12:11,080 --> 00:12:15,600
The drum has sounded,
marking the third watch.

94
00:12:16,720 --> 00:12:21,640
Your Majesty's yawning tells me...

95
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:26,280
it's time for you to rest.

96
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:43,240
If Your Majesty doesn't get enough sleep,
your health will suffer.

97
00:12:43,240 --> 00:12:44,800
The less you sleep,

98
00:12:44,800 --> 00:12:49,520
the weaker your body and immune system become.

99
00:12:49,520 --> 00:12:51,440
You'll be more prone to illness.

100
00:12:51,440 --> 00:12:56,120
Your memory and ability to think
may also suffer, Your Majesty.

101
00:12:56,920 --> 00:13:01,200
How do you know that?
Have you studied traditional medicine?

102
00:13:11,160 --> 00:13:15,400
A traditional healer in Wang Nam Lin
once told me my mother...

103
00:13:15,400 --> 00:13:17,880
fell ill from not getting enough sleep.

104
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:20,320
I've never forgotten it, Your Majesty.

105
00:13:31,720 --> 00:13:33,560
Let us retire for the night.

106
00:13:34,760 --> 00:13:40,480
I don't want anyone falling ill
from staying up late on my account.

107
00:13:42,720 --> 00:13:44,520
You may go and rest.

108
00:14:10,200 --> 00:14:12,400
<i>I'm worried that</i>

109
00:14:12,400 --> 00:14:19,320
<i>if Fongnuan, Saen Thep's wife's cousin,
becomes Father's favorite,</i>

110
00:14:19,320 --> 00:14:23,920
<i>your position as Crown Prince
could be threatened.</i>

111
00:14:37,520 --> 00:14:40,800
- I pay my respects to you, Your Majesty.
- I pay my respects to you, Your Majesty.

112
00:15:18,720 --> 00:15:20,200
Fongnuan.

113
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:41,560
You're fortunate His Majesty
wasn't offended tonight,

114
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:45,040
but you must be more careful
with what you say from now on.

115
00:15:47,720 --> 00:15:52,480
Forgive me for speaking out of turn.

116
00:15:57,400 --> 00:16:03,160
You told me my duty was to care for the King.

117
00:16:05,040 --> 00:16:09,240
If he fell ill from working late,

118
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:14,560
I'd have failed in my duty.

119
00:16:15,400 --> 00:16:19,160
Besides, you looked exhausted yourself.

120
00:16:19,160 --> 00:16:23,880
I couldn't let either you...

121
00:16:23,880 --> 00:16:26,000
or His Majesty fall ill.

122
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:29,920
Don't use me as an excuse.

123
00:16:30,680 --> 00:16:34,200
- Are you trying to flatter me?
- No, my lady.

124
00:16:35,240 --> 00:16:38,200
I'm genuinely concerned about you.

125
00:16:43,360 --> 00:16:46,440
I'm worried about myself, too.

126
00:16:47,600 --> 00:16:52,120
If anything happened to you, I'd be in trouble.

127
00:16:54,200 --> 00:16:55,920
I like your honesty.

128
00:16:57,040 --> 00:17:00,280
You never cease to surprise me.

129
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:08,200
But this is Wiang Kaew.
One wrong word could cost you your life.

130
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:09,680
Remember that.

131
00:17:12,560 --> 00:17:13,960
Yes, my lady.

132
00:17:15,360 --> 00:17:18,240
Why must I keep an eye on Fongnuan?

133
00:17:18,240 --> 00:17:22,040
She's only a lady-in-waiting.
She hardly seems dangerous.

134
00:17:22,040 --> 00:17:24,080
She's only a lady-in-waiting?

135
00:17:24,080 --> 00:17:27,480
How dare she tell the King
when to stop working and go to bed?

136
00:17:29,040 --> 00:17:32,880
An ordinary lady-in-waiting
would've been executed for that.

137
00:17:36,880 --> 00:17:39,960
Fongnuan has barely arrived at Wiang Kaew,

138
00:17:39,960 --> 00:17:43,120
yet Father already trusts her
and has grown fond of her.

139
00:17:44,760 --> 00:17:46,440
I don't trust her.

140
00:17:47,880 --> 00:17:51,000
I don't want Father
to take another royal consort.

141
00:17:55,480 --> 00:17:58,400
Father was probably just tired
and wanted to rest.

142
00:17:58,400 --> 00:18:00,120
Stop defending her.

143
00:18:02,160 --> 00:18:04,960
We still don't know where her loyalties lie.

144
00:18:05,520 --> 00:18:09,680
Homjan may have sent her to win Father's favor
for Kong Tai and Fah Haam,

145
00:18:10,680 --> 00:18:13,680
or Chiang La-or may be using her
to help Saen Thep gain power.

146
00:18:15,120 --> 00:18:20,560
Whichever side she's on,
I don't want another rival.

147
00:18:30,840 --> 00:18:33,440
Remember, she's the cousin of Saen Thep's wife.

148
00:18:34,920 --> 00:18:37,360
If I find out she's plotting anything,

149
00:18:39,280 --> 00:18:41,080
I won't spare her.

150
00:19:21,680 --> 00:19:23,560
<i>These orchids...</i>

151
00:19:25,480 --> 00:19:28,240
<i>will bloom in my heart...</i>

152
00:19:28,240 --> 00:19:30,640
<i>until my dying breath.</i>

153
00:20:21,560 --> 00:20:27,000
Has Princess Maneethip heard the news
about General In Saeng?

154
00:20:40,840 --> 00:20:43,680
I've learned about
Maneethip and General In Saeng.

155
00:20:47,240 --> 00:20:50,840
Don't be afraid to tell me the truth.

156
00:20:54,360 --> 00:20:57,360
I apologize on Princess Maneethip's behalf.

157
00:21:00,840 --> 00:21:03,320
She never meant to lie to you.

158
00:21:05,600 --> 00:21:09,400
She's been suffering over this all along.

159
00:21:10,880 --> 00:21:13,320
Please don't be angry with her.

160
00:21:26,160 --> 00:21:27,720
Don't be afraid.

161
00:21:29,600 --> 00:21:31,200
I understand.

162
00:21:33,800 --> 00:21:35,960
If anyone is to blame,

163
00:21:37,800 --> 00:21:39,760
I'm partly responsible.

164
00:22:01,120 --> 00:22:03,320
I'm going to Wiang Kaew today.

165
00:22:04,280 --> 00:22:09,120
Please make sure she eats when she wakes up.

166
00:22:09,880 --> 00:22:11,880
She hasn't eaten for days.

167
00:22:13,800 --> 00:22:15,160
I'm worried about her.

168
00:22:18,440 --> 00:22:19,720
Your Highness.

169
00:23:29,320 --> 00:23:31,200
I don't want to train.

170
00:23:31,840 --> 00:23:35,600
I don't like violence.
I don't like using force.

171
00:23:36,920 --> 00:23:39,280
Come on, Kong Tai.

172
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:46,320
What's this?

173
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:51,960
Why is the training so brutal?
I want no part of this.

174
00:23:51,960 --> 00:23:53,720
It's not worth dying for.

175
00:24:42,840 --> 00:24:44,160
A woman?

176
00:24:45,360 --> 00:24:46,840
Dao Kaew.

177
00:24:48,160 --> 00:24:50,600
Dao Kaew? You know her?

178
00:24:51,560 --> 00:24:54,600
Dao Kaew is Muen In's daughter.

179
00:24:55,400 --> 00:24:58,840
She's fought alongside her father and me.

180
00:24:58,840 --> 00:25:00,720
Of course I know her.

181
00:25:09,720 --> 00:25:13,800
What? Muen In lets his daughter go to war?

182
00:25:14,720 --> 00:25:18,240
He tried to stop her, but she wouldn't listen.

183
00:25:18,240 --> 00:25:21,920
She chose to live at the border,
and fight in the war.

184
00:25:21,920 --> 00:25:26,080
She's no good at household chores.
Fighting is what she does best.

185
00:25:29,760 --> 00:25:34,320
She's a better fighter
than almost anyone in the army.

186
00:25:39,160 --> 00:25:41,240
Muen In's daughter...

187
00:25:54,240 --> 00:25:57,960
- Why are you smiling, Brother?
- I'm not.

188
00:25:57,960 --> 00:26:00,760
- Are you training today or not?
- Of course.

189
00:26:00,760 --> 00:26:03,880
It's my duty. How could I refuse?

190
00:26:03,880 --> 00:26:06,480
I thought you didn't like violence.

191
00:26:06,480 --> 00:26:10,080
Being a soldier means fighting.
We must do our best to defend our homeland.

192
00:26:10,080 --> 00:26:15,760
I must always be ready to defend it.
Remember that.

193
00:26:17,200 --> 00:26:20,880
What are you waiting for? I'm ready.
Help me put on my armor.

194
00:26:25,720 --> 00:26:29,160
- Something must be going on.
- Yes.

195
00:26:29,960 --> 00:26:34,360
Dao Kaew rarely comes into the city.
What brings her here?

196
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:10,800
Prince Saen Thep.

197
00:27:32,320 --> 00:27:36,280
I saw this and thought of you.

198
00:27:38,440 --> 00:27:40,600
Perhaps it'll keep you company
when you're lonely.

199
00:27:41,840 --> 00:27:43,440
Thank you.

200
00:27:45,400 --> 00:27:49,800
I haven't had time to feel lonely.
There's so much work to do.

201
00:27:49,800 --> 00:27:51,960
I'm drowning in work!

202
00:27:55,840 --> 00:27:58,760
There I go using strange expressions again.

203
00:27:58,760 --> 00:28:00,200
That's good.

204
00:28:00,920 --> 00:28:03,000
You make me laugh.

205
00:28:03,000 --> 00:28:08,240
I haven't laughed once
since you moved into Wiang Kaew.

206
00:28:08,240 --> 00:28:10,160
I never thought...

207
00:28:10,160 --> 00:28:15,200
my silly remarks could be of use.

208
00:28:19,240 --> 00:28:22,480
I have a meeting
with Muen In and Seer Phrommaya.

209
00:28:24,120 --> 00:28:27,360
I'll be serving tea at that meeting.

210
00:28:28,000 --> 00:28:30,040
Lady Homjan ordered me to.

211
00:28:30,040 --> 00:28:33,480
Since I know all the princes,

212
00:28:33,480 --> 00:28:36,840
she asked me to attend to you
during the meeting.

213
00:28:38,520 --> 00:28:40,200
Then come with me.

214
00:28:40,200 --> 00:28:44,480
Not yet. I need to prepare the tea first.

215
00:28:45,920 --> 00:28:47,520
Let me help you.

216
00:29:10,720 --> 00:29:12,760
Did you know?

217
00:29:12,760 --> 00:29:16,200
Kong Tai loves this tea.

218
00:29:18,320 --> 00:29:22,000
What about you, Your Highness?
Do you like it?

219
00:29:23,520 --> 00:29:25,080
I do.

220
00:29:25,080 --> 00:29:27,240
Then have as much as you like.

221
00:30:19,920 --> 00:30:21,640
Please stop playing for a moment.

222
00:30:29,400 --> 00:30:31,720
What's gotten into Prince Kong Tai?

223
00:30:36,280 --> 00:30:38,640
He's showing all the signs of being in love.

224
00:30:41,120 --> 00:30:47,080
Kong Tai has met the woman of his dreams.
He's just found out she's Muen In's daughter.

225
00:30:49,360 --> 00:30:52,840
I see. The general's daughter.

226
00:31:03,920 --> 00:31:06,800
Hey! Why are you taking that away?

227
00:31:06,800 --> 00:31:11,200
Well, you were smiling to yourself,
staring dreamily at my rice.

228
00:31:11,200 --> 00:31:13,600
I thought you must be full.

229
00:31:13,600 --> 00:31:17,240
I've barely eaten anything!
How could I be full?

230
00:31:17,240 --> 00:31:22,440
Your heart is already
full of thoughts of Muen In's daughter.

231
00:31:23,520 --> 00:31:26,800
Wait, you know about Dao Kaew?

232
00:31:32,640 --> 00:31:34,760
So you admit it!

233
00:31:35,600 --> 00:31:39,640
- If you're full, I'll eat it myself.
- Wait!

234
00:31:40,880 --> 00:31:44,440
My heart may be full, but my stomach isn't!

235
00:31:44,440 --> 00:31:48,800
The happier I feel,
the better your food tastes.

236
00:31:48,800 --> 00:31:51,960
I'll eat every last bite. Please do.

237
00:31:52,840 --> 00:31:54,920
Let's see how long...

238
00:31:54,920 --> 00:31:59,360
you'll keep coming back for my food.

239
00:31:59,360 --> 00:32:00,960
Until the day I die.

240
00:32:00,960 --> 00:32:06,960
Even after I'm married,
I'll come back for your cooking every day.

241
00:32:09,520 --> 00:32:13,320
Being in love is wonderful, isn't it?

242
00:32:16,160 --> 00:32:20,200
That sticky rice looks sweet. Let me have some.

243
00:32:21,480 --> 00:32:23,400
Eat your own.

244
00:32:25,360 --> 00:32:28,080
Look! He's taking mine!

245
00:32:29,520 --> 00:32:33,880
Who's getting married again?
You're bickering like children.

246
00:32:36,280 --> 00:32:38,120
Let me try some.

247
00:32:42,880 --> 00:32:47,680
Prince Fah Haam.
This sticky rice tastes terribly bitter.

248
00:32:49,200 --> 00:32:51,120
Come on.

249
00:32:56,400 --> 00:32:58,400
It tastes sweet to me.

250
00:33:08,320 --> 00:33:11,200
Have you heard about General In Saeng?

251
00:33:16,080 --> 00:33:17,720
Your Highness...

252
00:33:19,880 --> 00:33:22,000
You know about him?

253
00:33:31,240 --> 00:33:32,920
He's dead.

254
00:33:40,880 --> 00:33:42,560
Has my cousin...

255
00:33:44,120 --> 00:33:46,240
heard the news?

256
00:33:54,320 --> 00:33:57,360
At least I finally know the truth.

257
00:34:00,080 --> 00:34:02,480
Maneethip should've told me from the start.

258
00:34:03,320 --> 00:34:07,200
If I'd known, I would've stepped aside.

259
00:34:09,120 --> 00:34:11,920
I don't have to get everything I want.

260
00:34:14,360 --> 00:34:15,960
My cousin...

261
00:34:17,240 --> 00:34:19,480
is the princess of Wang Nam Lin.

262
00:34:20,680 --> 00:34:25,560
She kept it from you
because she had a duty to fulfill.

263
00:34:25,560 --> 00:34:27,680
But she also owed me the truth.

264
00:34:28,320 --> 00:34:30,920
That's part of her duty as my consort.

265
00:34:40,040 --> 00:34:41,720
Your Highness,

266
00:34:44,840 --> 00:34:50,320
suppose you had a daughter one day.

267
00:34:51,480 --> 00:34:57,400
You wanted her to marry...

268
00:34:59,040 --> 00:35:02,800
as her duty required,
for the sake of her kingdom.

269
00:35:05,400 --> 00:35:08,720
But she was already in love with someone else.

270
00:35:08,720 --> 00:35:11,640
She wanted to marry him...

271
00:35:13,840 --> 00:35:19,840
and give up everything for a simple life,
without rank or power.

272
00:35:23,920 --> 00:35:29,400
She'd have to choose
between duty and happiness.

273
00:35:31,080 --> 00:35:33,360
Would you let her live that way?

274
00:35:42,680 --> 00:35:44,400
If it were my daughter,

275
00:35:46,880 --> 00:35:49,520
I know I'd love her dearly.

276
00:35:54,400 --> 00:36:00,200
I'd want her to be happy.
I'd let her live as she wished.

277
00:36:07,400 --> 00:36:09,800
Thank you.

278
00:36:09,800 --> 00:36:15,040
Talking to you has put my mind at ease.

279
00:36:19,520 --> 00:36:21,760
I'm worried about my cousin.

280
00:36:23,320 --> 00:36:25,600
How is she?

281
00:36:31,360 --> 00:36:35,520
What's done is done.

282
00:36:41,960 --> 00:36:46,880
As for what lies ahead, we must do our best.

283
00:36:48,320 --> 00:36:51,280
Don't worry about your cousin.

284
00:36:51,280 --> 00:36:56,760
Leave what we've discussed here,
and focus on your duties.

285
00:36:58,280 --> 00:37:04,280
I'll do the same
and take good care of your cousin.

286
00:37:49,840 --> 00:37:55,080
The King summoned me and reprimanded me
for failing to catch the rice bandits.

287
00:37:55,080 --> 00:37:58,480
Merng Mang's soldiers had to step in.

288
00:37:58,480 --> 00:38:01,600
But my men at the border insist...

289
00:38:01,600 --> 00:38:04,840
they've heard nothing of any rice bandits.

290
00:38:04,840 --> 00:38:06,920
If the bandits were real,

291
00:38:06,920 --> 00:38:10,840
my men would've known about them
before Merng Mang's soldiers did.

292
00:38:16,160 --> 00:38:21,560
Whenever I visit the border,
I hear nothing about these rice bandits.

293
00:38:21,560 --> 00:38:26,920
If our soldiers were patrolling there,
they would've arrived first.

294
00:38:27,600 --> 00:38:29,400
It's humiliating.

295
00:38:29,400 --> 00:38:34,360
Merng Mang's soldiers catching bandits
before ours?

296
00:38:34,360 --> 00:38:37,880
- It's unacceptable.
- I find it strange, too.

297
00:38:37,880 --> 00:38:41,080
Why would Merng Mang's soldiers suddenly
start catching bandits for us?

298
00:38:41,080 --> 00:38:43,120
Maybe they weren't bandits at all.

299
00:38:44,040 --> 00:38:45,960
Perhaps there's been a misunderstanding.

300
00:38:52,080 --> 00:38:55,000
What if someone deliberately misled us?

301
00:39:07,080 --> 00:39:09,280
If Fah Haam is right,

302
00:39:09,280 --> 00:39:15,000
Indraraja was the one who told Father
and sought recognition for Prince Pha Wiang.

303
00:39:15,000 --> 00:39:16,760
I doubt he's entirely unaware.

304
00:39:16,760 --> 00:39:20,200
Come now, Saen Thep. Of course he knows.

305
00:39:20,200 --> 00:39:23,920
If he knew and went along with it,
then he was part of the deception.

306
00:39:23,920 --> 00:39:26,320
I don't want to think that way,

307
00:39:26,320 --> 00:39:31,440
but I suspect Prince Pha Wiang is involved.

308
00:39:31,440 --> 00:39:35,520
If Prince Pha Wiang lied,
Indraraja must know about it.

309
00:39:35,520 --> 00:39:36,880
Don't you agree?

310
00:39:39,320 --> 00:39:43,520
Everyone knows
Ullavee's army is stronger than Merng Mang's.

311
00:39:43,520 --> 00:39:47,240
If they truly were bandits,
our soldiers couldn't have missed them.

312
00:39:58,760 --> 00:40:01,600
What are those two plotting?

313
00:40:08,600 --> 00:40:10,040
Could it be that...

314
00:40:13,920 --> 00:40:16,120
Indraraja deliberately lied?

315
00:40:20,880 --> 00:40:22,560
Forgive me, Your Highness.

316
00:40:31,640 --> 00:40:34,480
You're all gathered here.

317
00:40:35,680 --> 00:40:38,640
Is there something I should know?

318
00:41:36,440 --> 00:41:37,640
Fongnuan!

319
00:41:38,880 --> 00:41:40,320
Yes, Your Highness?

320
00:41:42,040 --> 00:41:46,760
If you hadn't stopped me,
I'd have kept talking.

321
00:41:46,760 --> 00:41:50,280
I'd have gotten into trouble
with Indraraja and Prince Pha Wiang.

322
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:53,280
That's what friends are for.

323
00:41:53,960 --> 00:41:56,960
You helped me before. I understand.

324
00:41:56,960 --> 00:42:00,040
But if you keep helping everyone
with every little thing,

325
00:42:00,040 --> 00:42:03,200
you might lose your head.

326
00:42:03,200 --> 00:42:04,600
Understood.

327
00:42:07,240 --> 00:42:10,160
I owe you one.

328
00:42:10,160 --> 00:42:14,960
If you ever need my help, just say the word.
I'll gladly help.

329
00:42:14,960 --> 00:42:18,280
Then do me a favor.

330
00:42:18,280 --> 00:42:22,480
Pay attention to who's around before you speak.

331
00:42:23,200 --> 00:42:26,160
I'd better finish cleaning up
before I get scolded.

332
00:42:26,160 --> 00:42:27,320
Please excuse me.

333
00:42:50,320 --> 00:42:53,400
The tea and dessert you prepared today...

334
00:42:55,360 --> 00:42:57,600
weren't to my liking.

335
00:42:57,600 --> 00:42:58,640
Really?

336
00:42:58,640 --> 00:43:03,680
But Prince Jom Harn told me
you liked rose tea and steamed banana cake.

337
00:43:10,520 --> 00:43:13,040
So you asked Jom Harn about my preferences.

338
00:43:14,880 --> 00:43:17,640
I just wanted to thank you...

339
00:43:17,640 --> 00:43:21,400
for showing me the way
to Wat Khao Nam Saeng the other day.

340
00:43:25,640 --> 00:43:31,160
Actually, I like
lotus tea and steamed banana cake.

341
00:43:35,840 --> 00:43:39,600
I like blue, but I don't like black.

342
00:43:41,720 --> 00:43:44,840
I like mangoes, but not vegetables.

343
00:43:44,840 --> 00:43:48,840
I like Hung Lay Curry. I don't like spicy food.

344
00:43:48,840 --> 00:43:54,840
I don't like getting drunk.
I prefer the scent of lotus to jasmine.

345
00:43:55,640 --> 00:43:59,840
I prefer rainy days to hot weather.

346
00:44:03,240 --> 00:44:08,040
I don't like seeing people cry.
I hate insincere people.

347
00:44:17,040 --> 00:44:22,080
Next time, don't ask anyone else.
If you want to know something, ask me.

348
00:44:42,880 --> 00:44:46,960
How did senior get it so wrong? He's hopeless.

349
00:44:46,960 --> 00:44:48,200
He gave me away.

350
00:45:10,640 --> 00:45:12,080
Where do you think you're going?

351
00:45:17,080 --> 00:45:21,640
I met with my brothers today
about the rice thefts at the border.

352
00:45:21,640 --> 00:45:25,160
I'd like to investigate this myself.

353
00:45:26,600 --> 00:45:28,160
I forbid you to go.

354
00:45:35,920 --> 00:45:39,120
Why, Mother? This is a serious matter.

355
00:45:39,120 --> 00:45:44,440
If we don't put a stop to these bandits,
they'll raid our granaries again.

356
00:45:44,440 --> 00:45:48,160
We'll run short of rice,
and our people will suffer.

357
00:45:50,360 --> 00:45:54,120
If you keep working all the time,
when will you find a wife?

358
00:45:58,640 --> 00:46:00,760
- A wife?
- Yes.

359
00:46:02,200 --> 00:46:07,600
This is important.
You need a consort to please your father.

360
00:46:13,800 --> 00:46:18,560
If no one has caught your eye,
I'll find someone for you.

361
00:46:22,240 --> 00:46:24,480
Leave the border matter alone for now.

362
00:46:26,160 --> 00:46:27,440
I've arranged for you

363
00:46:27,440 --> 00:46:30,760
to meet
daughters of noble and prominent families.

364
00:46:34,760 --> 00:46:36,920
Don't embarrass me.

365
00:46:48,440 --> 00:46:53,160
Pha Wiang has already caught the rice bandits.

366
00:46:53,160 --> 00:46:55,160
That should've settled the matter.

367
00:46:56,280 --> 00:46:58,280
Why discuss it again?

368
00:47:01,480 --> 00:47:03,880
Muen In called everyone together...

369
00:47:03,880 --> 00:47:05,760
to discuss

370
00:47:05,760 --> 00:47:09,880
why Ullavee's soldiers at the border
knew nothing about the rice thefts.

371
00:47:10,760 --> 00:47:13,520
When Pha Wiang and I entered
the Royal Library,

372
00:47:13,520 --> 00:47:15,760
why did everyone fall silent?

373
00:47:17,600 --> 00:47:21,120
Muen In must be embarrassed...

374
00:47:21,120 --> 00:47:26,040
that Ullavee's soldiers failed
to secure the border.

375
00:47:26,040 --> 00:47:30,160
He's probably trying to avoid blame
by placing it on someone else.

376
00:47:30,160 --> 00:47:35,720
Seeing us together must
have left him too ashamed to speak his mind.

377
00:47:35,720 --> 00:47:36,760
As for the others,

378
00:47:36,760 --> 00:47:41,360
I doubt they wanted to trouble you
over such a minor matter.

379
00:47:42,120 --> 00:47:43,480
That seems likely.

380
00:47:43,480 --> 00:47:47,280
No wonder they fell silent,
and didn't know what to say.

381
00:47:47,280 --> 00:47:49,240
Your influence must have intimidated them.

382
00:47:51,720 --> 00:47:53,360
We mustn't let our guard down.

383
00:47:54,360 --> 00:47:57,440
Everyone in Wiang Kaew is watching us.

384
00:47:57,440 --> 00:48:01,400
We must watch what we say and do.

385
00:48:22,520 --> 00:48:24,760
Under the circumstances,

386
00:48:24,760 --> 00:48:30,480
I'm sure you know
what you should and shouldn't say.

387
00:48:34,520 --> 00:48:35,920
Don't worry.

388
00:48:36,640 --> 00:48:39,360
I won't get myself into trouble.

389
00:48:40,680 --> 00:48:45,160
You'd better not cause trouble
for Indraraja either.

390
00:48:46,160 --> 00:48:48,960
Or I won't be the only one without a homeland.

391
00:48:52,960 --> 00:48:58,400
The throne of Merng Mang could slip
from your grasp as well.

392
00:49:30,800 --> 00:49:32,200
Mother.

393
00:49:33,200 --> 00:49:35,040
Is this really necessary?

394
00:49:38,280 --> 00:49:42,440
I'm finding you a consort.
I won't let you be outdone.

395
00:49:47,640 --> 00:49:51,240
This is Ked Kaew. She's Saen Inta's daughter.

396
00:49:51,240 --> 00:49:53,760
Her family has held
the title of Supreme Minister

397
00:49:53,760 --> 00:49:54,960
for generations.

398
00:49:54,960 --> 00:50:00,680
If you take her as your consort,
her family will give you great support.

399
00:50:06,800 --> 00:50:10,160
This is La-ong Kham.
She's Muen Kaew's daughter.

400
00:50:10,160 --> 00:50:11,920
Her father is the Senior Military Minister.

401
00:50:11,920 --> 00:50:14,120
His rank is below the Supreme Minister's,

402
00:50:14,120 --> 00:50:17,400
but his family comes
from a long line of royal artisans

403
00:50:17,400 --> 00:50:19,560
and is highly respected.

404
00:50:24,160 --> 00:50:26,280
This is Bua Wai.

405
00:50:26,280 --> 00:50:31,640
Her father is Kham Tan,
the wealthiest merchant in Ullavee.

406
00:50:31,640 --> 00:50:35,360
Her family may not be of noble birth,

407
00:50:37,200 --> 00:50:42,440
but her wealth would certainly benefit you.

408
00:50:48,160 --> 00:50:52,880
All these women come from influential families
that could support you.

409
00:50:54,320 --> 00:50:56,840
Whichever one you choose,

410
00:50:56,840 --> 00:51:00,160
she'll be just as worthy
as Saen Thep's consort.

411
00:51:20,840 --> 00:51:25,520
You can't escape it, however hard you try.
How can anyone live without love?

412
00:51:30,240 --> 00:51:31,560
True.

413
00:51:32,160 --> 00:51:36,000
But being in love doesn't mean
you'll get what you want.

414
00:51:36,000 --> 00:51:40,040
Every time I fall in love,
I end up disappointed.

415
00:51:40,040 --> 00:51:45,840
At least neither of you
is being controlled like I am.

416
00:51:45,840 --> 00:51:49,720
Didn't any of the women
Royal Consort Sukantha chose for you

417
00:51:49,720 --> 00:51:51,680
catch your eye?

418
00:51:53,080 --> 00:51:54,600
I don't know...

419
00:51:54,600 --> 00:52:00,360
what it feels like to be attracted
to someone or to fall in love.

420
00:52:02,240 --> 00:52:06,040
Could you two explain how I can tell...

421
00:52:06,040 --> 00:52:09,840
whether I'm in love?

422
00:52:11,320 --> 00:52:13,280
It's simple.

423
00:52:13,280 --> 00:52:17,120
You meet someone
you can't get out of your mind.

424
00:52:22,520 --> 00:52:28,280
Whether you're asleep or awake, eating or resting,
you keep thinking of them.

425
00:52:28,960 --> 00:52:32,960
When they smile, you smile too.

426
00:52:32,960 --> 00:52:37,160
When they laugh, you laugh too.

427
00:52:38,560 --> 00:52:43,880
If I had to choose between falling in love
and catching bandits,

428
00:52:46,240 --> 00:52:48,280
I'd rather hunt bandits.

429
00:52:50,280 --> 00:52:52,200
I'm off to the border.

430
00:52:56,440 --> 00:52:57,720
Jom Harn!

431
00:53:06,240 --> 00:53:08,120
Lady Fongnuan.

432
00:53:11,680 --> 00:53:14,120
Where's my cousin? How is she?

433
00:53:14,120 --> 00:53:17,640
Please go upstairs, my lady.
Prince Saen Thep is waiting.

434
00:53:40,880 --> 00:53:42,600
Cousin.

435
00:53:50,160 --> 00:53:51,760
What's wrong with her?

436
00:53:53,240 --> 00:53:55,120
Ever since Maneethip heard the news,

437
00:53:57,000 --> 00:53:59,520
she hasn't left her room.

438
00:54:00,400 --> 00:54:02,240
She refuses to eat.

439
00:54:16,320 --> 00:54:17,720
Cousin.

440
00:54:26,120 --> 00:54:27,720
Fongnuan.

441
00:54:28,520 --> 00:54:31,880
I heard you weren't feeling well,

442
00:54:31,880 --> 00:54:35,240
so I asked Lady Homjan
for permission to come and care for you.

443
00:54:36,800 --> 00:54:41,800
Please eat something and take your medicine.
You'll feel better soon.

444
00:54:46,480 --> 00:54:48,440
I have no appetite.

445
00:55:07,760 --> 00:55:10,040
Stay here and keep her company.

446
00:55:10,960 --> 00:55:15,040
I'll bring some snacks
and a fresh dose of medicine.

447
00:55:21,000 --> 00:55:26,480
Seeing you might give her
the strength to get up and eat.

448
00:56:47,680 --> 00:56:50,160
Where are all the maids?

449
00:56:55,520 --> 00:56:59,080
I sent them to prepare her medicine
and to the market...

450
00:56:59,080 --> 00:57:03,120
for Maneethip's favorite fruits and snacks.

451
00:57:05,520 --> 00:57:10,360
I've come to get some warm water.
I want to give her a sponge bath.

452
00:57:13,760 --> 00:57:15,320
Your Highness!

453
00:57:16,360 --> 00:57:21,640
Let me have a look.
I'll put some ointment on it.

454
00:57:34,600 --> 00:57:39,360
Thank you on Maneethip's behalf.

455
00:57:47,960 --> 00:57:50,000
Why are you thanking me?

456
00:57:51,440 --> 00:57:54,280
Even though she's hurt you,

457
00:57:56,320 --> 00:57:59,000
you're still taking such good care of her.

458
00:58:01,360 --> 00:58:04,040
How could I not thank you?

459
00:58:09,800 --> 00:58:12,520
I've hurt her too.

460
00:58:14,440 --> 00:58:17,080
She may be suffering more than I am.

461
00:58:18,840 --> 00:58:20,840
Her grief has made her ill.

462
00:58:27,880 --> 00:58:30,840
I'm truly grateful, Your Highness.

463
00:58:38,880 --> 00:58:43,760
I can't change what's happened.

464
00:58:47,320 --> 00:58:49,560
But from this day forward,

465
00:58:51,800 --> 00:58:57,200
I'll do everything I can
to take good care of Maneethip.

466
00:59:00,480 --> 00:59:02,280
Once she recovers,

467
00:59:05,040 --> 00:59:07,400
whatever she decides,

468
00:59:10,520 --> 00:59:12,080
I'll accept her decision.

469
00:59:17,760 --> 00:59:19,160
In that case,

470
00:59:20,960 --> 00:59:24,360
let's do everything we can for her...

471
00:59:25,080 --> 00:59:30,320
and help her get well as soon as possible.

472
00:59:43,880 --> 00:59:45,800
Once upon a time, in a forest,

473
00:59:47,040 --> 00:59:50,880
all the animals lived together in harmony.

474
01:01:06,720 --> 01:01:10,320
[Next Week]
<i>You have a lot on your mind right now,</i>

475
01:01:10,320 --> 01:01:11,920
<i>especially about your cousin.</i>

476
01:01:11,920 --> 01:01:13,600
<i>You've been looking after everyone else.</i>

477
01:01:13,600 --> 01:01:15,320
<i>Don't forget to take care of yourself.</i>

478
01:01:15,320 --> 01:01:17,200
<i>Whatever the future holds,</i>

479
01:01:17,200 --> 01:01:22,320
<i>I'll devote the rest of my life
to taking good care of you and your cousin.</i>

480
01:01:23,720 --> 01:01:26,840
<i>I'm sorry I wasn't there for you
when you were suffering.</i>

481
01:01:26,840 --> 01:01:29,280
<i>Dao Kaew. Don't you remember me?</i>

482
01:01:29,280 --> 01:01:30,520
<i>You're that drunkard.</i>

483
01:01:30,520 --> 01:01:34,120
<i>You asked Lady Homjan to arrange for me
to teach you music, didn't you?</i>

484
01:01:34,120 --> 01:01:37,200
<i>- Yes.
- Do you want to see me more often?</i>

485
01:01:37,200 --> 01:01:39,640
<i>Princess Maneethip's condition
has grown much worse.</i>
